<title>USA: GaSonics wins $10 mln in orders.</title>
<headline>GaSonics wins $10 mln in orders.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>GaSonics International Corp, a supplier of semiconductor processing equipment, on Tuesday said it has received $10 million worth of orders from two semiconductor makers in Asia.</p>
<p>In a statement, GaSonics said the orders are for its Performance Enhancement Platform systems that are used to make dynamic random access memory (DRAM) chips with 0.35 micron design rules.</p>
<p>GaSonics shares ended up 1/2 at 19.</p>
</text>
